# workflows/molab/.env.example -- copy to workflows/molab/.env and fill in.
#
# env.sh sources the first of ${MOLAB_ENV_FILE}, workflows/molab/.env and the
# .env one level above the checkout (/marimo/.env) that exists. The real .env is
# gitignored: it holds credentials, and this repo's .gitignore does not
# otherwise cover it.
#
#   cp workflows/molab/.env.example workflows/molab/.env
#   $EDITOR workflows/molab/.env
#   source workflows/molab/env.sh

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# GitHub token, for pushing the working branch. molab has no persistent disk,
# so commits that live only on the box are lost when the session ends.
# Needs `repo` scope (or `public_repo` for a public fork). Create at
# https://github.com/settings/tokens
# GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_...

# The GitHub account the token belongs to, used for the commit trailer and the
# credential helper. Not a secret.
# GITHUB_USER=emattei

# ── The molab bucket (setup_molab.sh) ────────────────────────────────────────
# Private: the container, the build files and the d0 test data live here.
# GCP_SA_JSON is the service-account key file's CONTENTS as one quoted line of
# JSON, not a path. setup_molab.sh mints a read-only token from it with openssl
# and never writes it to disk. Never commit a real key.
# GCP_BUCKET="broad-nnfc-molab"
# GCP_SA_JSON='{"type":"service_account","client_email":"...","private_key":"<PEM, newlines as \\n>","...":"..."}'

# ── Where results are archived ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# The bucket is public to READ but not to write, so this needs
# `gcloud auth login` -- a token here is not enough.
# MOLAB_GCS_DEST=gs://broad-buenrostro-pipeline-genome-annotations/chrombpnet/test_data_d0

# ── Box-specific ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The REAL core count. The box reports the host's (20+), not the slice you get.
# MOLAB_CPUS=4
# DATASET=d0
# REFERENCE_ROOT=/marimo/data/references
